ment Loss Of Approximately $2.2 Billion Related To Pension & Opeb Plans', 'text': 'FORD MOTOR CO - FOR QUARTER ENDED DEC 31, 2019, EXPECT TO RECORD PRE-TAX REMEASUREMENT LOSS OF APPROXIMATELY $2.2 BILLION RELATED TO PENSION & OPEB PLANS.FORD MOTOR CO - EXPECTED PRE-TAX REMEASUREMENT LOSS FOR QUARTER ENDED DEC. 31 INCLUDESA $2.0 BILLION LOSS ASSOCIATED WITH PENSION PLANS OUTSIDE U.S..FORD MOTOR CO - REMEASUREMENT LOSS DID NOT HAVE AN IMPACT ON OUR CASH IN 2019, AND DOES NOT CHANGE OUR EXPECTATIONS FOR PENSION CONTRIBUTIONS IN 2020.FORD MOTOR CO - EXPECTED PRE-TAX REMEASUREMENT LOSS FOR QUARTER ENDED DEC. 31 INCLUDES $600 MILLION LOSS ASSOCIATED WITH OPEB PLANS GLOBALLY.FORD MOTOR CO - ON AFTER-TAX BASIS, REMEASUREMENT LOSS IS EXPECTED TO REDUCE NET INCOME BY ABOUT $1.7 BILLION FOR QUARTER ENDED DECEMBER 31, 2019.FORD - INCLUDING IMPACT OF REMEASUREMENT GAINS, LOSSES, EXPECT UNDERFUNDED STATUS FOR PENSION & OPEB PLANS AT 2019 END  OF ABOUT $6.8 BILLION & $6.1 BILLION.'}{'symbol': 'FCX', 'date': '2020-01-23 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Freeport-Mcmoran Reports Q4 Adjusted Earnings Per Share $0.02', 'text': "FREEPORT-MCMORAN REPORTS FOURTH-QUARTER AND YEAR ENDED 2019 RESULTS.Q4 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.02.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $-0.00 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FREEPORT-MCMORAN- CONSOLIDATED SALES FOR 2020 ARE EXPECTED TO APPROXIMATE 3.5 BILLION POUNDS OF COPPER, 0.8 MILLION OUNCES OF GOLD, 88 MILLION POUNDS OF MOLYBDENUM.QTRLY REVENUE $3.91 BILLION VERSUS $3.68 BILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.Q4 REVENUE VIEW $3.70 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.AT DEC 31, 2019, CONSOLIDATED DEBT TOTALED $9.8 BILLION AND CONSOLIDATED CASH TOTALED $2.0 BILLION.QTRLY AVERAGE REALIZED PRICE PER POUND FOR COPPER $2.74 VERSUS $2.75.CAPITAL EXPENDITURES TOTALED $0.7 BILLION (INCLUDING ABOUT $0.4 BILLION FOR MAJOR PROJECTS) IN Q4 2019.Q4 COPPER SALES OF 906 MILLION POUNDS WERE 4 PERCENT HIGHER THAN OCTOBER 2019 ESTIMATE OF 870 MILLION POUNDS.QTRLY AVERAGE REALIZED PRICE PER OUNCE FOR GOLD $